    "title": "Tootsies announces grand opening date - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By No media credit provided. ,\n1 days ago\nBAY COUNTY, Fla. ( WMBB ) – The long-awaited Tootsie’s Orchid Lounge grand opening is set.\nThe lounge, which used to be located in Pier Park, is now located at the former Spinnaker’s Beach Club property.\nThe new location was brought about by a deal between Spinnaker owner, Sparky Sparkman, and Toostie’s owner, Steve Smith.\nIt was originally reported that Tootsie’s was set to open back in February, but the date had to be pushed back.\nThe official grand opening weekend is set for May 1 and 2, featuring Randy Houser and Riley Green as guest musicians. More musicians are planned to be announced.\nTootsie’s has VIP reservations available for their opening weekend. To book a table, click here .\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to mypanhandle.com.",
